One main package with two directives that each produce more than one record at one
site: one naming two codes above a live declaration, and one above a specification
that declares two names. Both are stale at every record, so a run measures that the
findings collapse by site.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/selfcheckcollapse

go 1.27.1
-- main.go --
package main

func main() { println(loud(), first, second) }

//deadset:ignore DS1001,DS1101 -- stale at both codes: main reaches loud
func loud() string { return "l" }

var (
	//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- stale at one code and two declarations
	first, second = 1, 2
)
